  "source_context": {
    "pdf_page": 22,
    "full_page_text": "169\n BMRCL/Phase-3/JPN-MRS/Demolition/DLN-P1/2026/157       Employer Requirement, Scope of Work &\n                                                                       Technical Specifications\n\n\n             ANNEXURE -3 to EMPLOYER’S REQUIREMENT\n                            (To be submitted by Tenderer)\n\n              MINIMUM PLANTS & EQUIPMENTS FOR THE WORK\n\n                 (TO BE DEPLOYED AS AND WHEN REQUIRED)\n\n     Tenderers should have the following plant and machinery either owned or leased or hired\n     by him.\n\n\n         Sl.\n            Type of equipment required for the work     Proposed to be deployed\n     No\n\n       1   Diamond disc Cutter/floor saw machine with              3 Nos\n               suitable capacity\n       2    Wall Sawing Machine with suitable capacity               3 Nos\n\n       3     Electric Drill Motors/ Hammer drilling                    4 Nos\n            machine\n\n       4    Floor Saw Machine with suitable capacity                4 Nos\n\n       5    Chipping Machine                                   12 Nos\n\n       6    Crusher/Combi Crusher                              2 Nos\n\n       7    Hydraulic Mobile crane                               2 Nos\n\n       8    High/Long Reach Demolition equipment as               1 Nos\n             per the requirement\n       9    Hydraulic rock breaker with loader                      2 Nos\n\n      10  DG set 100kV or higher capacity                       2 Nos\n\n\n  NOTE:\n       1.  Plant and Equipment indicated above is minimum to be deployed at appropriate stage\n           of the work. However, depending on the requirement to complete the work in the\n           stipulated completion period, the tenderer should deploy additional machinery as\n         circumstances warrant at no extra cost.\n       2.  Plant and equipment to be mobilized for the work shall be in good serviceable\n           condition.\n\n\n\n\n\nBangalore Metro Rail Corporation Ltd.                 September 2026           Section Page 19 of 37",
